$DIR/test.p:4:22: a default value cannot refer to parameter t (defaults are evaluated by the caller)
    A default value is evaluated by the caller, in the scope where the function
    is declared, before the function runs. The function's parameters do not
    exist yet at that point, so a default cannot use them.
    Default to a sentinel value instead, and compute the real value in the body.
    (see "Default parameter values" in the Plutonium spec, section 10.13)
    (run "pluto explain E2205" for a longer explanation)
